# Master cases

What the Master may do at which status, read while `master.mode` is not `off`. Copy this file to `master-cases.md` to
edit a case; a case your copy lacks is read from here. A move at a status no case names is not made: it is written to
`misses.jsonl` beside `state.json` instead, and the task stops for you. `master.mine` and `humanPaths` still keep a
move yours where a case allows it.

Each case: `move:` a verb the Master presses or a step it sends the session · `at:` the task's statuses, `any` or
`any but <statuses>` · `by: master` · one line saying what the case is. What the session may answer is its own case's,
in `session-cases.md`.

## ship

move: ship
at: REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the hand-back, it holds, and the Master ships it.

## reply

move: reply
at: REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
On the Master's ship the session posts its drafted replies to the reviewers.

## deploy

move: deploy
at: REVIEWED, APPROVED
by: master
The request is green with every thread closed, and the Master deploys it once.

## deploy-finish

move: deploy
at: DEPLOY_CONFLICT
by: master
The session staged a deploy conflict resolved in full, and the Master finishes the deploy you pressed.

## approve-plan

move: approve-plan
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: master
The Master read the plan, it holds, and the Master approves it.

## add-repo

move: add-repo
at: any but DONE
by: master
The session asked for a repository its task lacks, and the Master adds it.

## round-not-ready

move: round-not-ready
at: REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
The Master sends its findings on the hand-back to the session.

## plan-not-ready

move: plan-not-ready
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: master
The Master sends its findings on the plan to the session.

## asked-human

move: asked-human
at: PLAN_PENDING, REVIEW_PENDING
by: master
The Master asked you a question and tells the session to wait on the answer.

## plan-answered

move: plan-answered
at: PLAN_PENDING
by: master
The Master answers the question a plan was handed back with.

## answered

move: answered
at: any but PLAN_PENDING, SHIPPING, DEPLOY_CONFLICT, DONE
by: master
The Master answers a session's question.

## answered-under

move: answered-under
at: SHIPPING, DEPLOY_CONFLICT
by: master
The Master answers a session's question below the instruction it still works on.
